# oApogee output allowlist
#
# THIS IS THE PASSIVE PAYLOAD BOUNDARY. Read this file to confirm it without
# reading any C.
#
# Every physical output the firmware is permitted to drive appears here, one per
# line, with the schematic reference designator, the pin label it lands on, and
# what it is for. There are exactly two. Both exist to help a person find a
# rocket or to tell a person what the payload is doing.
#
# oApogee does not fire ejection charges, control deployment, ignite motors, or
# command any pyrotechnic device. There is no output on this list that could, and
# there is no output that is not on this list.
#
# HOW THIS FILE IS ENFORCED
#
# The check-outputs build target compares this list, name for name, against the
# oa_out_t enumerators in port/include/oapogee_port/oa_out.h. Adding an output to
# either one alone fails the build. Adding one to both is a change to the passive
# payload boundary, and that is a project decision made in the open, not a
# firmware change made in passing.
#
# WHAT IS NOT ON THIS LIST, AND WHY
#
# Bus and peripheral lines (I2C, SPI, UART, QSPI, and the radio) are not on this
# list. They are declared in port/include/oapogee_port/oa_port.h. They carry
# bytes to parts soldered to the board, and none of them is a general purpose
# output a builder could connect something to. The property this list protects is
# that no output exists that could be wired to an igniter.
#
# The radio deserves its own sentence. It transmits and never receives: there is
# no receive function in the port layer at all. A ground station cannot arm this
# payload, cannot trigger anything, and cannot deploy anything, because there is
# no code path from the air into this firmware.
#
# NOTHING HERE HAS RUN ON HARDWARE. No board has been fabricated.
#
# Format: NAME  designator  pin  purpose
# Lines beginning with # and blank lines are ignored.

OA_OUT_BUZZER      LS1  BUZZER               Piezo transducer, externally driven, so the firmware generates the waveform. Arm indication, and the recovery beacon pattern after landing. On a Solo build it is the only recovery aid there is.
OA_OUT_STATUS_LED  D1   LED_R,LED_G,LED_B    RGB LED, common cathode, three pins through series resistors R10 to R12. Shows flight state and fault conditions to a person standing next to the rocket. Three pins, one output: this list is about capability, not wire count.
